**Definition 1.3 (what the four names mean).** Space observes the current
rooted ordered material and the field currently on its vertices. Time
observes the actual selected successful-generation chronology, including
the requested Tick gaps in A and the prescribed attached clocks in C.
Boundary observes the earned terminal positions together with the sampled
terminal data at their actual epochs. Memory observes an earned current
code and a finite block of predictions for future autonomous terminal
responses under a fixed interpreter. It contains neither an unrestricted
chronicle nor a table of answers to arbitrary future controls.

Sections 5 and 11 specify these observations precisely on one jointly
reached image for each installation. All four use the same actual source
binding, control installation and current rights. A recovered numerical
description is not a newly obtained reference or grant. Historical
recoverability is asserted only on the specified images; full current
service is defined on a broader rational state domain.

